{20}{He was an... intriguing person. Frightening, all the same. His was a crazed and dread aura of fear. When he walked into the Inn,  even if you didn't notice him come in, something felt wrong in the air, like a bad taste in the back of your throat that you can't identify. He wore a black hat like a preacher, and a dusty, faded black suit with a black cloak. And he had eyes like a wolf.}{He was an... intriguing person. Frightening, all the same. His was a crazed and dread aura of fear. When he walked into the Inn,  even if you didn't notice him come in, something felt wrong in the air, like a bad smell you can't identify, only it doesn't smell. He wore a black hat like a preacher, and a dusty, faded black suit with a black cloak. And he had eyes like a wolf.}{}{}{}{}
{21}{Wow. Who did he talk to here in town?}{}{5}{}{25}{}
{22}{Ya... who talk wit him?}{}{-4}{}{25}{}
{23}{F:}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{25}{Well, we know he visited the Landers household, and we haven't seen the Landers since. So you'll probably find some clues there. Oh, and he spoke with Bill Sprecklethorpe. No one knows what about, but probably magical dealins, seein' as how Bill's the town Magicker and all. In any case, we think he's headed to Tull via the Portlandia Bridge. [He shows you where Tull and Portlandia are on your map.]}{Well, we know he visited the Landers household, and we haven't seen the Landers since. So you'll probably find some clues there. Oh, and he spoke with Bill Sprecklethorpe. No one knows what about, but probably magical dealins, seein' as how Bill's the town Magicker and all. In any case, we think he's headed to Tull via the Portlandia Bridge. [He shows you where Tull and Portlandia are on your map.]}{}{}{}{mm4 ,mm6 }
{26}{What can you tell me about Tull?}{}{5}{}{40}{}
{27}{What 'bout Tull?}{}{-4}{}{40}{}
{28}{Do you know anything of Portlandia?}{}{5}{}{35}{}
{29}{What yoo know bout Portlandia?}{}{-4}{}{35}{}
{30}{Well, thank you for the information. I'd like to speak to you about something else...}{}{5}{}{1}{}
{31}{Ok, thank you much. Um, me want talk 'bout something else.}{}{-4}{}{1}{}
{34}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{35}{Portlandia USED to be a city, long ago... now it's just ruins strewn amidst the great bridges that stand there, connecting each shore to the center island. Magnificent sight.}{Portlandia USED to be a city, long ago... now it's just ruins strewn amidst the great bridges that stand there, connecting each shore to the center island. Magnificent sight.}{}{}{}{}
{36}{Let's talk about something else...}{}{5}{}{1}{}
{37}{We talk bout something else now.}{}{-4}{}{1}{}
{40}{Tull? It's a tiny little town, almost a ghost town, to the north. Once, it had some copper veins being mined nearby, and so it grew to a small township, but now it's mostly abandoned. It lies very close to the Black Mountains, however, and not many folk know much about the other side of those mountains, beyond what they hear in fairy tales. So maybe Walter's goal lies across those mountains. It looks like he's heading as far away from Gilead as possible, to be honest.}{Tull? It's a tiny little town, almost a ghost town, to the north. Once, it had some copper veins being mined nearby, and so it grew to a small township, but now it's mostly abandoned. It lies very close to the Black Mountains, however, and not many folk know much about the other side of those mountains, beyond what they hear in fairy tales. So maybe Walter's goal lies across those mountains. It looks like he's heading as far away from Gilead as possible, to be honest.}{}{}{}{}
{41}{What is your opinion of the Kingdom of Gilead?}{}{5}{}{60}{}
{42}{Can you tell me 'bout Gilead?}{}{-4}{}{60}{}
{43}{Can you show me where Tull is?}{}{5}{}{45}{}
{44}{Kan yoo show me ware Tull iz??}{}{-4}{}{45}{}
{45}{Let me mark it on your map for you...[He points to it on your map.]}{Let me mark it on your map for you...[He points to it on your map.]}{}{}{}{}
{46}{Thanks. I'd like to talk to you about something else...}{}{5}{}{1}{}
{47}{Okie. Now, 'bout the other stuffs...}{}{-4}{}{1}{}
{48}{Can you tell me about Gilead?}{}{5}{}{60}{}
{49}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{60}{Gilead is the finest nation in all of the world, friend. Her borders stretch as far as the eye can see, so far that some of these towns don't even know what nation they belong to. [He smiles.] It's true! Some of them go generations without any contact with the rest of the kingdom. Makes it difficult when tax time comes around, but they appreciate it when they be needin to call on the militia.}{Gilead is the finest nation on all of the world, friend. Her borders stretch as far as the eye can see, so far that some of these towns don't even know what nation they belong to. [He smiles.] It's true! Some of them go generations without any contact with the rest of the kingdom. Makes it difficult when tax time comes around, but they appreciate it when they be needin to call on the militia.}{}{}{}{}
{61}{Continue.}{}{5}{}{65}{}
{62}{You tell me more.}{}{-4}{}{65}{}
{63}{F:}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{64}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{65}{The Kingdom of Gilead is ruled by a King, 'tis true. But he is kept in balance with the elected Lord's High Council, who review his actions and decrees, as he reviews theirs. And they are each also checked in power by the Council- elected Lord High Judge, who leads the courts and can declare the other branches' decrees invalid under the basis of infringing upon the rights of a person. A good system overall, and it keeps our government from being to harsh upon us.}{The Kingdom of Gilead is ruled by a King, 'tis true. But he is kept in balance with the Lord's High Council, who review his actions and decrees, as he reviews theirs. And they are each also checked in power by the Council- elected Lord High Judge, who leads the courts and can declare the other branches' decrees invalid under the basis of infringing upon the rights of a person. A good system overall, and it keeps our government from being to harsh upon us.}{}{}{}{}
{66}{Please, tell me more.}{}{1}{}{70}{}
{67}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{70}{The current ruler of Gilead is King Tristan II, who is descended of Tristan I, descended of Jeneman III, who was the last ruler to engage in any serious expansion of the Kingdom. Right now, the Inner Baronies are the only ones that are directly affected by the Crown. There is too much happening in the Kingdom right now and the Crown's influence and men are spread too thinly across the land. The outlying Baronies are getting restless and there's even been talk of revolution in some places. But not here, we're still loyal to our Lord here.}{The current ruler of Gilead is King Tristan II, who is descended of Tristan I, descended of Jeneman III, who was the last ruler to engage in any serious expansion of the Kingdom. Right now, the Inner Baronies are the only ones that are directly affected by the Crown. There is too much happening in the Kingdom right now and the Crown's influence and men are spread too thinly across the land. The outlying Baronies are getting restless and there's even been talk of revolution in some places. But not here, we're still loyal to our Lord here.}{}{}{}{}
{71}{Thanks. Let's talk about something else...}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{72}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{80}{Well, I hear Mr. Tyrell, in the shop south of here, has got himself an adventure of some kind cooked up. He always did have a bit of the wanderer about him, though. Also, Geofram Gilliam, the local maintenance technician and hardware salesman, has a job for an adventurer. You can find him to the northwest of here. You could also try George Doan's, up north.}{Well, I hear Mr. Tyrell, in the shop south of here, has got himself an adventure of some kind cooked up. He always did have a bit of the wanderer about him, though. Also, Geofram Gilliam, the local maintenance technician and hardware salesman, has a job for an adventurer. You can find him to the northwest of here. You could also try George Doan's, up north.}{}{}{}{}
{81}{Thanks for the information, Alaron. Back to what you were saying earlier...}{}{5}{}{1}{}
{82}{Okie. Me want to talk 'bout somethin else.}{}{-4}{}{1}{}
{83}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{100}{Hello! @pcname@, is it? I recognized you from the description the Council telegraphed us. I most heartily welcome you to Newberg, the jewel of the western kingdom! My name is Aloran, and I am the Liaison to the Kingdom of Gilead here in town, as well as the town spokesperson. I'm very pleased to have a squire of Gilead in our little town, and I hope you do enjoy your stay.}{Hello! @pcname@, is it? I recognized you from the description the Council telegraphed us. I most heartily welcome you to Newberg, the jewel of the western kingdom! My name is Aloran, and I am the Liaison to the Kingdom of Gilead here in town. I'm very pleased to have a squire of Gilead in our little town, and I hope you do enjoy your stay.}{}{}{}{}
{101}{I thank you, Liaison, for your hospitality. Although your town is pleasant and peaceful, I fear my stay shall be short. I am here on urgent business.}{}{5}{}{110}{gf13 1}
{102}{Errrr, ya, thanks for bein nice to me. I here for find da Man in Black. You know where he gone?}{}{-4}{}{110}{gf13 1}
{103}{Shut up, pissant. I'll do the talking here. You tell me where I can find this... Walter. The Man in Black. Quickly, where is he?}{}{5}{}{120}{gf13 1}
{104}{You shut up, little stupid man! You do what I sez, and I sez you tell me where to find Man in Black!!}{}{-4}{}{120}{gf13 1}
{105}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{gf13 1}
{110}{Ah yes, ugly business, that, sir. The man you seek, Walter, was here for but a few hours. He has nearly a day on you already. He set out on the High Road, north, to Tull.}{Ah yes, ugly business, that, lady. The man you seek, Walter, was here for but a few hours. He has nearly a day on you already. He set out on the High Road, north, to Tull.}{}{}{}{}
{111}{Damn. Well, I have some questions to ask you before I head out.}{}{5}{}{1}{}
{112}{Oh. Well, me gots stuff to ask 'fore I go.}{}{-4}{}{1}{}
{113}{Hmm. Thanks. Good bye.}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{120}{Sir, I do not brook insults well. If you wish to make an enemy of me, continue speaking thus. If you wish our relationship to be of a combative nature, then speak so again. If you would have peace with me, and work together as we have been so instructed by our Lord High Council, then I beg of you to speak as a friend.}{Ma'am, I do not brook insults well, and it does not speak well of you as a lady. If you wish to make an enemy of me, continue speaking thus. If you wish our relationship to be of a combative nature, then speak so again. If you would have peace with me, and work together as we have been so instructed by our Lord High Council, then I beg of you to speak as a friend.}{}{}{}{}
{121}{I apologize for my words. This trip has been stressful and I have let it get the best of me.}{}{5}{}{130}{}
{122}{Me sorry. Me grumpy-grumpy today, brain hurt from too much thinking.}{}{-4}{}{130}{}
{124}{Sod off, you overdramatic buzzard-hound. I shit bigger than you. You can suck a fatty.}{}{5}{}{}{co}
{125}{Fuck you, ugly stupid dumb penis head!! You shut up}{}{-4}{}{}{co}
{126}{Good bye.}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{130}{Aye, it's a terrible case and I understand the pressure you're under. Your words are forgotten. Anyway, as I was saying, Walter, the Man in Black, left heading north, we understand, to the township of Tull. }{Aye, it's a terrible case and I understand the pressure you're under. Your words are forgotten. Anyway, as I was saying, Walter, the Man in Black, left heading north, we understand, to the township of Tull. }{}{}{}{}
{131}{Hmmm...let me ask you something else.}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{132}{Good bye.}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{150}{Heh, not much to tell, sir. I grew up here in Newberg, and I love this town so much that when I joined the Gilead Diplomat Corps, I just stayed on here and became Liaison to Newberg. Then when the Airships needed a place to fuel and perform maintenance out here, I offered Newberg immediately because I knew how much it would help this town out. We have a great place here, and I'm glad I was able to help it grow.}{Heh, not much to tell, sir. I grew up here in Newberg, and I love this town so much that when I joined the Gilead Diplomat Corps, I just stayed on here and became Liaison to Newberg. Then when the Airships needed a place to fuel and perform maintenance out here, I offered Newberg immediately because I knew how much it would help this town out. We have a great place here, and I'm glad I was able to help it grow.}{}{}{}{}
{151}{Haven't you ever wanted to leave?}{}{5}{}{160}{}
{152}{You been here your hole life? You don't wanna leave or nuthin?}{}{-4}{}{160}{}
{153}{Good. Rot here.}{}{1}{}{0}{re -10}
{154}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{160}{I suppose I have, at one time or another... but I like this town an awful lot. And I won't follow a green commander. I'm no babysitter.}{I suppose I have, at one time or another... but I like this town an awful lot. And I won't follow a green commander. I'm no babysitter.}{}{}{}{}
{161}{Well, would you like to come with me, assist me in my quest?}{}{5}{le 10}{180}{}
{162}{Well, would you like to come with me, assist me in my quest?}{}{5}{le -9,le5 }{170}{}
{163}{You come wit me? We do crazy fun stuff!}{}{-4}{le 10}{180}{}
{164}{You come wit me? We do crazy fun stuff!}{}{-4}{le -9,le5 }{170}{}
{165}{F:}{}{1}{}{}{}
{170}{I'm sorry, but you're not an able enough commander yet. Gain some more field experience, and I'll reconsider.}{I'm sorry, but you're not an able enough commander yet. Gain some more field experience, and I'll reconsider.}{}{}{}{}
{171}{About what you said earlier...}{}{1}{}{1}{}
{172}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{180}{Ok! You seem like just the type of commander I'd like to work under. It will be an honor, sir.}{Ok! You seem like just the type of commander I'd like to work under. It will be an honor, madam.}{}{}{}{}
{181}{Wonderful! Follow me.}{}{5}{}{0}{jo 0 0}
{182}{Ok, we go now.}{}{-4}{}{0}{jo 0 0}
{200}{Newberg is a great little town. We have the local Inn, the Rusty Doorknob, run by widow Engstrom, over on the east side, and we've got the General Store, run by old Erenor, on the west side of town. Then you've got the weapons salesman Mr. Tyrell, to the south, and the hardware salesman and repairman, Geofram Gilliam, to the northwest. Of course, you've got the Airship port, where we're standing, and then there's George Doan, the town Historian. His house's up north.}{Newberg is a great little town. We have the local Inn, the Rusty Doorknob, run by widow Engstrom, over on the east side, and we've got the General Store, run by old Erenor, on the west side of town. Then you've got the weapons salesman Mr. Tyrell, to the south, and the hardware salesman and repairman, Geofram Gilliam, to the northwest. Of course, you've got the Airship port, where we're standing, and then there's George Doan, the town Historian. His house's up north.}{}{}{}{}
{201}{Thanks for the tips. About what you mentioned earlier...}{}{5}{}{1}{}
{202}{Okie, thanks. We talk 'bout other stuff now...}{}{-4}{}{1}{}
{203}{Do you know anything else about Newberg?}{}{5}{}{210}{}
{205}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{210}{Newberg is an affiliated city-state within the Kingdom of Gilead. As such, they have to have a representative of the Kingdom as their head of government. That would be my position, the Liaison. However, all the legislation I pass is based on votes put up in town meetings here in the Meeting Hall. It's a very efficient system.}{Newberg is an affiliated city-state within the Kingdom of Gilead. As such, they have to have a representative of the Kingdom as their head of government. That would be my position, the Liaison. However, all the legislation I pass is based on votes put up in town meetings here in the Meeting Hall. It's a very efficient system.}{}{}{}{}
{211}{Interesting. Back to what you said earlier...}{}{5}{}{1}{}
{212}{Me not understand any of dat. Now 'bout wut yoo sed earlier?}{}{-4}{}{1}{}
{213}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{250}{Well, what kind of weapon were you looking for? A gun? A sword? An Axe? What?}{Well, what kind of weapon were you looking for? A gun? A sword? An Axe? What?}{}{}{}{}
{251}{Gun.}{}{1}{}{260}{in-2203 }
{252}{Sword.}{}{1}{}{260}{in-2204 }
{253}{Axe}{}{1}{}{260}{in-2205 }
{260}{Okay. Here you go, then. Did you need something else?}{Okay. Here you go, then. Did you need something else?}{}{}{}{}
